{"id":"word:hebrew:H7563","type":"word","title":"רָשָׁע","subtitle":"H7563 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"morally wrong ; concretely, an (actively) bad person","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to רָשָׁע (H7563) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 263 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"רָשָׁע (râshâʻ) means morally wrong ; concretely, an (actively) bad person First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 8 32."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"רָשָׁע","transliteration":"râshâʻ","pronunciation":"raw-shaw'","strong":"H7563","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7563","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["רְשָׁעִ֣ים","רָשָׁ֑ע","רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים","רָ֭שָׁע","רְ֭שָׁעִים"],"morphs":[["HAampa",105],["HAamsa",93],["HTd/Aamsa",9],["HRd/Aamsa",9],["HTd/Aampa",8],["HC/Aampa",7],["HR/Aamsa",7],["HC/Aamsa",5],["HR/Aampa",5],["HRd/Aampa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"morally wrong ; concretely, an (actively) bad person","usage":"condemned, guilty, ungodly, wicked (man), that did wrong.","full":"H7563. rasha רָשָׁע 263 adjective wicked, criminal ; — absolute ׳ר Gen 18:23 +; plural רְשָׁעִים Isa 13:11 +; construct רִשְׁעֵי Psa 75:9 3 t. feminine singular רְשָׁעָה Ezek 3:18 (strike out Co), 3:19 ( רָשָׁע Co); — 1 usually as substantive , one guilty of crime , deserving punishment; sometimes also wicked ; opposed to צַדִּיע ; רָשָׁע Exod 2:13 ; 23:1 (E), Deut 25:2 ; Prov 17:23 ; 18:5 ; 25:5 ; Job 9:22 , 24 ; collective Gen 18:23 , 25 (twice in verse) (J) Micah 6:10 ; Prov 3:33 ; 28:4 , רשׁעים 1Sam 24:14 ; Jer 5:26 ; Prov 19:28 ; 20:26 ; 29:12 , רשׁעים אנשׁים 2Sam 4:11 (murderers), לָמוּת רָשָׁע Num 35:31 (P) guilty of death , ר ׳מוֺשֵׁל Prov 28:15 , compare 29:2 , ר ׳הִצְדִּיק Exod 23:7 (E) Isa 5:23 ; Prov 17:15 ; ר ׳הִרְשִׁיעַ Deut 25:1 ; 1Kin 8:32 = לְרָשָׁע השׁיב 2Chr 6:23 ; לר ׳אמר צַדִּיק Prov 24:24 . 2 guilty of hostility to God or his people, wicked enemies: רשׁע singular Psa 17:13 6 t. Psalms; Isa 26:10 ; collective Psa 9:6 ; 9:17 ; 10:2 6 t. Psalms; Isa 11:4 ; Hab 3:13 ; רשׁעים Psa 3:8 ; 7:10 ; 9:18 5 t. Psalms; Isa 48:22 ; 57:20-21 , Jer 25:31 ; Ezekiel 21:34; Malachi 3:21 ( + (possibly) other cases; often hard to decide); specifically of Pharaoh Exod 9:27 (J), Babylon Isa 13:11 ; 14:5 , Chaldeans Hab 1:4 , 13 ; || יהוה שׂנְאֵי 2Chr 19:2 . 3 guilty of sin , against either God or man, wicked: הרשׁעים האנשׁים Num 16:26 (J, rebellious Korahites), Mal 3:18 (not serving ׳י ), opposed to צַדִּיק ; singular individual Ezek 3:18 (twice in verse); 21:30 ; 33:8 (twice in verse); Psa 11:5 ; 32:10 ; Prov 9:7 +; collective Isa 3:11 ; Job 34:18 ; 36:6 , 17 ; plural רשׁעים Isa 53:9 ; Jer 23:19 = 30:23 , Zeph 1:3 ; Psa 26:5 ; Prov 10:3 ; Eccl 8:10 +; || חסֹידים 1Sam 2:9 (Poem), Psalm 12:9; Psa 50:16 ; 97:10 ; 145:20 ; || תוֺדָתֶ֑ךָ עֹזְבֵי 119:53 ; compare V:61, +; ר ׳אדם Prov 11:7 ; Job 20:29 ; 27:13 ; ר ׳אִישׁ Prov 21:29 ; ר ׳מלאך 13:17 ; רשׁעים זֶרַע Psa 37:28 ; רשׁעים עֲצַת 1:1 ; Job 10:3 ; 21:16 ; 22:18 ; רשׁעים דֶּרֶךְ Jer 12:1 ; Psa 1:6 ; 146:9 ; Prov 4:19 ; 12:26 ; רשׁע דֶּרֶךְ 15:9 ; הָֽרְשָׁעה מִדַּדְכּוֺ Ezek 3:18-19 , (but see, Co, above); (ה)ארץ רִשְׁעֵי Psa 75:9 ; 101:8 ; 119:119 ; Ezek 7:21 ( ᵐ5 Co עריצי ). — is rare before exile; chiefly Ezekiel Psalms Wisdom Literature.","rootNote":"from 7561 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 8 32","keyReferences":["1Kgs 8 32","1Sam 2 9","2Chr 6 23","2Chr 19 2","2Sam 4 11","Dan 12 10","Dan 12 10","Deut 25 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":263,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 8 32","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"רָשָׁ֔ע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HAamsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 9","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/רְשָׁעִ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Aampa"},{"reference":"2Chr 6 23","book":"2Chr","chapter":6,"verse":23,"engl